      "claim": "Lamivudine, another pyrimidine dideoxynucleoside, has absolute F of 87% (solution), 69±9%, 81±19%, 68.6±11%, 93±15%, and 86±17% across doses and formulations, all above 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C04", "C06", "C15", "C20", "C23", "C24"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Zalcitabine, a pyrimidine dideoxynucleoside with a dideoxy sugar, has absolute F of 80% (54-127%) in humans and 30% in fasted mice, both above 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C17", "C28"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Didanosine and cladribine are less transferable purine nucleoside contexts; their F values (22-29% and 36-46%) are at or above 20%, and didanosine's variable/low average does not provide affirmative evidence for F<20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C03", "C09", "C11", "C14", "C25", "C27", "C07", "C12", "C16"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Theophylline records show high oral bioavailability for a small polar heterocycle, consistent with but not decisive for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C02", "C08", "C29"]
    },
